  "homeActivities": [
    {
      "text": "Activity 1 — Taste needs smell\nCover his eyes and ask him to hold his own nose closed. Give him a small piece of apple, then a small piece of potato or pear. He will barely\ntell them apart! Now let him release his nose — suddenly the taste appears. Smell and taste work together.\nActivity 2 — Who has the biggest hand?\nThis is his first real measuring. Two ways:\n• Fill a bowl with dried beans. Each person takes one handful and counts them. The biggest hand holds the most.\n• Or trace each person's hand on squared paper and count the squares inside.\nThen put the results in a simple table. He is learning to measure, record and compare — the skill behind all science.",
      "safety": "An adult stays with the child for every activity. No glass, no sockets, no flames, and nothing small enough to swallow is left with a child\nalone. Water activities are done in a bowl or the sink, never near electrical items.",
      "pages": [
        8,
        9,
        10
      ],
      "safetyPages": [
        2
      ]
    }
